Track 3: The Rhizome Room
- Story & Context: Years later, the legendary 'Rhizome Room' in what was once Dr. Mensah's lab became a pilgrimage site for artists seeking the genre's true essence, though its true power was only felt when a rare bioluminescent fungus bloomed on the walls, resonating with the room's deep bass, causing the very air to vibrate with a palpable, electric charge during live sets. Visitors recounted visions of interconnected roots stretching across the globe, whispered through the sub-bass: "We are all just nodes in the grand network." The room, more than a studio, became a living organism, a conduit for the world's hidden botanical symphony.
